implementationPlan.description:
Tests, part 1 (base allow-list), one file: moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/util/RuntimeSelectionPolicyTest.kt.
- Change no existing row. That includes 526a2080's N5-N7 and S7-S8 and 1c2bfeca's N8 and S9.
- New rows are N9, N10, S10 and S11.
- Methods that need Windows start with `assumeTrue("Windows path forms", RuntimeSelectionPolicy.windowsHost)`, and they must RUN on the verification host.
- Paths below are runtime spellings; write them as Kotlin literals with doubled backslashes.
- Where a row installs a fake drive lookup, capture the default first (`val native = RuntimeSelectionPolicy.driveType`) and put it back before the row's controls. @After resetForTest also restores it.

Helpers, placed next to share() and nonLocalSpellings():
1. nonLocalBases(project: File): List<String>. Let real = realFile(project).path (`X:\rest`) and s = share("localhost", project). Return listOfNotNull of:
   - s and share("127.0.0.1", project);
   - s with '\' replaced by '/', which is IntelliJ's `//localhost/X$/rest`;
   - `\\wsl$\moe-no-such-distro\proj` and `\\wsl.localhost\moe-no-such-distro\proj`;
   - `\\localhost\moe-no-such-share$\proj`, a missing share;
   - real.substring(2), the rooted form;
   - real.substring(0, 2) + real.substring(3), the drive-relative form;
   - `<real>\..\<project.name>` and `<real>\.`;
   - `<real>.`, a trailing dot;
   - `<real> `, a trailing space; JDK 17's Paths.get throws on it, so the raw check must refuse it first;
   - volumeSpelling(project), which is nullable.
   Its KDoc says the rule must never look any of these up.
2. rawJunction(link: File, target: String): Boolean. It makes a mount point at the empty folder link whose substitute name is exactly `\??\` + target. Port it from D:\arch-52fb-r3-probe\Junction.java (rawJunction), which was proven on JDK 17.0.20:
   - link.mkdir();
   - Kernel32.INSTANCE.CreateFile(link.path, WinNT.GENERIC_WRITE, 0, null, WinNT.OPEN_EXISTING, WinNT.FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS or WinNT.FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT, null);
   - a com.sun.jna.Memory REPARSE_DATA_BUFFER: tag WinNT.IO_REPARSE_TAG_MOUNT_POINT, ReparseDataLength = 8 + path bytes, the substitute name at offset 0, then the print name (target), each UTF-16LE and NUL-terminated;
   - DeviceIoControl(handle, WinioctlUtil.FSCTL_SET_REPARSE_POINT, …), with CloseHandle in finally.
   Any failure answers false. KDoc: mklink /J and PowerShell New-Item -ItemType Junction normalize a trailing '.' out of the target (probe), so the reparse point is written directly. A mount point on an empty folder you own needs no privilege.
3. withDottedJunction(name, body: (link: File, dotted: String) -> T): T. Steps:
   - dotted = realFile(temporaryFolder.root).path + '\' + name + '.';
   - create dotted with exitOf("cmd", "/c", "mkdir", `\\?\` + dotted). Java's Paths.get rejects '?', and Win32 would drop the dot;
   - link = File(temporaryFolder.root, "$name-link"); assertTrue that rawJunction(link, dotted) succeeds;
   - run body;
   - in finally, delete link (File.delete removes only the reparse point), then exitOf("cmd", "/c", "rd", "/s", "/q", `\\?\` + dotted). JUnit's TemporaryFolder cannot delete a dot-ending folder, because Win32 reads `name.` as `name`.

N9, pure predicate, runs on every host like N5. isPlainLocalPath(windows = true):
- is false for:
  - `C:\x\project.` and `C:\x\project.\bin`;
  - `C:\x\project ` and `C:\x\project \bin`;
  - `C:\x\..\proj` and `C:\x\.\proj`;
  - `C:\x\...`;
  - `\\?\C:\x\project.` and `c:/x/project./bin`;
- is true for `C:\x\project.d\bin`, `C:\x\.hidden\bin`, `C:\x\a b\c` and `C:\x\v1.2.3`.
With windows = false, `/w/project.` and `/w/x/../y` stay true.

N10, isOutsideProject, Windows.
Setup:
- project = newFolder("project"), with bin/ created;
- outside = newFolder("outside");
- store = ProtectedStateStore(temporaryFolder.root.toPath().resolve("system/moe/protected-state"));
- untouched = { throw AssertionError("looked up $it") }. It is an Error, so the catches cannot swallow it;
- driveType = { throw AssertionError("drive type of $it") }.
For every base in nonLocalBases(project):
- for every path in [project.path, File(project, "bin").path, File(project, "missing").path, outside.path], assertFalse both with resolve = untouched and with the default resolve;
- assertFalse(store.usableFor(base)). Comment that this is an accepted cost: that project's protected state stays session-only.
LEGACY keeps today's answer, with the throwing drive lookup still installed: when volumeSpelling(project) is not null, isOutsideProject(outside.path, volumeBase, RuntimeProfile.LEGACY) is true.
Then restore the default lookup. With it:
- isOutsideProject(outside.path, project.path, resolve = { outside.toPath().resolve("nodejs.").resolve("bin") }) is false. This is the candidate real path with a dot segment: without the segment rule, identity would keep it.
- Controls: isOutsideProject(bin, project.path) is false, outside.path is true, and store.usableFor(project.path) is true.

S10, selection and spawn, Windows.
Setup:
- (project, root, node) = protectedFixture();
- planted = File(project, "node"), containing "planted";
- sandbox = installedLayout(File(project, "build/idea-sandbox/plugins/moe-jetbrains"));
- volumeBase = volumeSpelling(project), guarded by assumeTrue(volumeBase != null) as S8 does;
- reason = BASE_NOT_PLAIN's text;
- a throwing drive lookup, as in N10.
For every base:
- assertEquals(reason, assertRejected(…)) for installedExecutable(planted.path, base), installedExecutable(node.path, base), installedArtifact(sandbox, "daemon/index.js", base) and installedArtifact(root, "daemon/index.js", base). The outside pair proves that the base check refuses, not identity.
- Set env PATH to node.parentFile.path, project.path and the project's bin. After supervisorFor(project, { null }, { null }).protectedDaemonEnvironment(env, base), env equals mapOf("PATH" to "").
Spawn through volumeBase, which is local, so no SMB. Let message = "Protected execution profile: $reason. Project and PATH copies of the Moe daemon are not used." For supervisorFor(File(volumeBase), { root }, { node.path }, started = started, statuses = statuses):
- ensureDaemonRunning() is false;
- started is empty;
- statuses == listOf(false to message);
- selectionRefusal() == message;
- stopCommandOrNull(volumeBase) is null.
LEGACY, still with the throwing lookup: supervisorFor(File(volumeBase), { root }, { node.path }, profile = { RuntimeProfile.LEGACY }).stopCommandOrNull(volumeBase) equals listOf(realFile(node).path, realFile(File(root, "daemon/index.js")).path, "stop", "--project", volumeBase).
Control, after restoring the default lookup: installedExecutable(node.path, project.path) == Accepted(realFile(node)).

S11, a junction to a literal `project.`, Windows. Setup:
- `(_, root, node) = protectedFixture()`;
- project = newFolder("project"), with File(project, "node") containing "planted";
- store as in N10;
- inside withDottedJunction("project"), write File(link, "node") with "node". It lands in `project.`.
Hazard, with comments: File(dotted, "node").readText() is "planted". The real path read back is the project's file, while File(link, "node") reads "node".
Candidate side:
- installedExecutable(File(link, "node").path, project.path) is refused with exactly "node executable is not a plain local Windows path";
- isOutsideProject(link.path, project.path) is false.
Base side:
- installedExecutable(node.path, link.path) and installedArtifact(root, "daemon/index.js", link.path) are refused with exactly BASE_NOT_PLAIN's text;
- isOutsideProject(node.parentFile.path, link.path) is false;
- store.usableFor(link.path) is false.
Controls:
- installedExecutable(node.path, project.path) == Accepted(realFile(node));
- isOutsideProject(node.parentFile.path, project.path) is true.

End the step with one GREEN targeted run under the jetbrains-gradle lease (see step 4 for the command). The RED runs come in step 4.

Tests, part 2 (drive type), plus RED and GREEN for every new check. Same file: moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/util/RuntimeSelectionPolicyTest.kt.

S12, a base on a drive that is not local, Windows. Setup:
- (project, root, node) = protectedFixture();
- outside = node.parentFile;
- driveRoot = the project's drive root `X:\` (project.path.substring(0, 2) plus a backslash);
- seen = mutableListOf<String>();
- message as in S10.
Install each of these lookups in turn; every one records its argument in seen:
- one that answers WinBase.DRIVE_REMOTE;
- one that answers DRIVE_UNKNOWN;
- one that answers DRIVE_NO_ROOT_DIR;
- one that throws IllegalStateException;
- one that throws UnsatisfiedLinkError, a LinkageError, as when JNA cannot load.
For each:
- installedExecutable(node.path, project.path) and installedArtifact(root, "daemon/index.js", project.path) are refused with exactly BASE_NOT_PLAIN's text;
- isOutsideProject(outside.path, project.path) is false;
- protectedDaemonEnvironment with PATH = outside.path gives mapOf("PATH" to "");
- a fresh supervisorFor(project, { root }, { node.path }, started = started, statuses = statuses): ensureDaemonRunning() is false, started is empty, statuses == listOf(false to message) and selectionRefusal() == message.
For each local type (DRIVE_REMOVABLE, DRIVE_FIXED, DRIVE_CDROM, DRIVE_RAMDISK), again recording:
- installedExecutable(node.path, project.path) == Accepted(realFile(node));
- isOutsideProject(outside.path, project.path) is true.
Then assert that seen is not empty and that every entry equals driveRoot, ignoring case. The lookup only ever gets the drive root, never a UNC or a full path.
LEGACY, with a lookup that throws AssertionError:
- supervisorFor(project, { root }, { node.path }, profile = { RuntimeProfile.LEGACY }).stopCommandOrNull(project.path) equals listOf(realFile(node).path, realFile(File(root, "daemon/index.js")).path, "stop", "--project", project.path);
- isOutsideProject(outside.path, project.path, RuntimeProfile.LEGACY) is true.
Default lookup in this JVM (proves step 2), after restoring the default:
- driveType(driveRoot) is one of the four local types;
- for the first letter from Z down to D whose root does not exist, driveType of that root is not a local type. A free or disconnected letter is never local. Skip only that assertion when every letter exists.

RED, then GREEN. Run every one under the jetbrains-gradle lease (moe.acquire_resource, released at the end) with: cmd.exe /d /c "set GRADLE_OPTS=-Xmx512m&& cd /d D:\projexts\moes\moe-jetbrains && .\gradlew.bat test --rerun --tests com.moe.util.RuntimeSelectionPolicyTest"
- RED-1: make both base checks pass (each isPlainLocalBase call in isOutsideProject and select answers true). N10, S10, S11's base side and S12 must fail.
- RED-2: put isPlainLocalPath back to drive-qualified only. N9 must fail. S11 must fail: the candidate reason becomes 'resolves inside the project', and the base is accepted. The '..', '.', trailing '.' and trailing ' ' bases in N10 and S10 must fail.
- RED-3: let isPlainLocalBase skip the drive lookup. S12 must fail.
- GREEN: restore everything. The class passes, and N9, N10, S10, S11 and S12 executed without <skipped/>.
Record, in the step note, the rows each RED run failed, and the GREEN count.

